## MCP Mutation Surface

Call `tools/list` first. It returns the effective supported production tool
set for the current token after capability, repository-scope, and production
visibility filters. Local workflow-file authoring methods and retired dogfood
composites are hidden from discovery. `tools/call` re-authorizes every call;
mutating calls append metadata-only audit rows, including denials.

Use `workflow.generate.preview` before any workflow write when it appears in
`tools/list`. Workflow-file authoring writes use the web-chat
workflow-authoring flow or CLI compatibility fallback and may not be
discoverable through production daemon MCP `tools/list`.

Recover from `capability_missing`, `token_revoked`, `token_expired`,
`method_unknown`, and `mutations_disabled` by stopping and asking the
operator for the narrow correction named by the denial.
